Vendored UNMODIFIED
===================

`skills/` (11 skills and their `references/`), `commands/` (2 commands),
`LICENSE`, `logo.svg`, and `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` are copied byte-for-byte.
Unlike `plugins/datadog`, nothing here needed adapting: these skills teach how to
build on Cloudflare (Workers, Durable Objects, Agents SDK, Wrangler, web
performance) rather than how to configure an MCP client, so they carry no
client-specific server ids, config paths, or UI instructions. No skill declares
`allowed-tools`, so none of them narrows the tool list on load.

Added by Corepass
=================

- `.corepass-plugin/plugin.json` — our manifest. Upstream's omits `displayName`,
  which the storefront needs, so the plugin would otherwise render as the bare
  slug `cloudflare`.
- `.mcp.json` — REPLACED, not copied. Same five servers and URLs as upstream at
  this commit; rewritten only so this file stays ours to edit.
- `README.md` — ours, describing the packaging.

Not vendored
============

- `.github/` (Semgrep workflow), `CODEOWNERS`, `.gitignore` — repository tooling,
  excluded per this repo's "leave CI and build tooling behind" rule.
- `.cursor-plugin/` — Cursor's manifest and marketplace index; our loader probes
  `.corepass-plugin` then `.claude-plugin`, so it would never be read.
- `rules/workers.mdc` — a Cursor `.mdc` rule file. Corepass has no `rules`
  component, so it would be inert here.
- Upstream's `README.md` — replaced with ours rather than kept alongside.

Note on the two commands: their frontmatter carries
`allowed-tools: [Read, Glob, Grep, Bash, Write, Edit, WebFetch]`, which are Claude
Code's tool names, not ours (`read_file`, `glob`, `grep`, `run_command`,
`write_file`, `edit_file`, `web_fetch`). This is harmless — `CommandEntry`
surfaces `allowed_tools` to the inventory for display only and never enforces it
as a tool allowlist, unlike a skill's `allowed-tools`, which does become a real
`tool_allowlist`. Left verbatim so the copy stays diffable against upstream.
